      "description": "Whether the scenes' lamps (point, spot and area lights) are shaded through the engine's clustering: the view cut into cells, each with the lamps that reach it (`Scene.punctualLightClustering`, the engine's default). Without it every mesh shades the lamps that reach it, which costs less with a few lamps. The clustering keeps its lamp lists in textures sized to the lamps in the view: one coming into or leaving the view (a lamp scrolled out with its card) has the engine make them all anew, a frame of about 30 ms on an iPhone.",
